---
const currentYear = new Date().getFullYear();
const yearDisplay = currentYear === 2026 ? "2026" : `2026 - ${currentYear}`;
---
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href="/favicon.svg" />
    <title>Terms of Service &middot; bcaupper.cafe</title>
    <style>
        :root {
            --bg: #ffffff;
            --text: #111111;
            --muted: #666666;
            --border: #eaeaea;
        }

        * {
            box-sizing: border-box;
            margin: 0;
            padding: 0;
        }

        body {
            background-color: var(--bg);
            color: var(--text);
            font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, "Segoe UI", Roboto, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;
            font-size: 16px;
            line-height: 1.6;
            padding: 40px 20px;
            max-width: 580px;
            margin: 0 auto;
        }

        header {
            margin-bottom: 32px;
        }

        h1 {
            font-size: 1.25rem;
            font-weight: 600;
            letter-spacing: -0.02em;
            margin-bottom: 8px;
        }

        p {
            color: var(--muted);
            margin-bottom: 20px;
            font-size: 0.95rem;
        }

        hr {
            border: none;
            border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
            margin: 28px 0;
        }

        .section-title {
            font-size: 0.8rem;
            text-transform: uppercase;
            letter-spacing: 0.05em;
            color: var(--muted);
            margin-bottom: 12px;
            font-weight: 600;
        }

        ul {
            list-style: none;
            margin-bottom: 20px;
        }

        li {
            margin-bottom: 8px;
            font-size: 0.95rem;
            color: var(--muted);
        }

        li::before {
            content: "• ";
            color: var(--muted);
        }

        a {
            color: var(--text);
            text-decoration: underline;
            text-underline-offset: 3px;
            text-decoration-color: #d1d1d1;
        }

        a:hover {
            text-decoration-color: var(--text);
        }

        .back-nav {
            margin-bottom: 24px;
            font-size: 0.85rem;
        }

        footer {
            margin-top: 40px;
            font-size: 0.85rem;
            color: var(--muted);
        }

        footer nav {
            margin-top: 12px;
            display: flex;
            gap: 12px;
        }

        footer nav a {
            color: var(--muted);
            font-size: 0.85rem;
        }
    </style>
</head>
<body>

    <nav class="back-nav">
        <a href="/">&larr; Back to bcaupper.cafe</a>
    </nav>

    <header>
        <h1>Terms of Service</h1>
        <p>Last updated September 2026</p>
    </header>

    <main>
        <div class="section-title">1. Acceptance & Permitted Purpose</div>
        <p>
            By visiting or accessing bcaupper.cafe, the web application (app.bcaupper.cafe), or any affiliated native mobile applications (collectively, the "Platform"), you agree to be bound unconditionally by these Terms of Service.
        </p>
        <p>
            The Platform is developed solely by Kabir Sekhon as an independent academic software project. It is managed and intended exclusively for the use of active students, faculty, and authorized staff of Bergen County Academies ("BCA") in Hackensack, New Jersey. Any unauthorized, malicious, commercial, or automated scraping use is strictly prohibited.
        </p>

        <hr />

        <div class="section-title">2. Absolute Disclaimer of Warranties ("As-Is")</div>
        <p>
            The Platform and all associated code, data, endpoints, teacher absence records, and check-in rosters are provided strictly on an <strong>"AS-IS"</strong> and <strong>"AS-AVAILABLE"</strong> basis without warranty of any kind, whether express, implied, statutory, or otherwise.
        </p>
        <p>
            Neither Kabir Sekhon nor any affiliated developer warrants that the Platform will operate uninterrupted, error-free, timely, secure, or that absence rosters or attendance logs will always be accurate or synchronized with official school district records. Users and students remain independently responsible for adhering to official school policies and reporting to class or study hall.
        </p>

        <hr />

        <div class="section-title">3. Complete Limitation of Liability (Kabir Sekhon)</div>
        <p>
            Under no circumstances and under no legal theory (whether in contract, tort, negligence, strict liability, product liability, or otherwise) shall the developer, <strong>Kabir Sekhon</strong>, be liable to you, Bergen County Academies, Bergen County Technical Schools, or any third party for any direct, indirect, incidental, consequential, special, punitive, or exemplary damages.
        </p>
        <p>
            This complete liability exclusion applies to any damages including, but not limited to: loss of attendance status, disciplinary citations, academic penalties, data corruption or loss, service interruptions, server failures, hardware malfunction, unauthorized access, or any reliance placed upon absence listings or check-in confirmations.
        </p>

        <hr />

        <div class="section-title">4. Mobile App Publishing & Entity Shield (SAVERA CONTINENTAL LIMITED)</div>
        <p>
            The mobile applications associated with the Platform may be distributed, packaged, or hosted in mobile application stores (e.g., Apple App Store, Google Play Store) under the publisher organization entity <strong>SAVERA CONTINENTAL LIMITED</strong>.
        </p>
        <p>
            SAVERA CONTINENTAL LIMITED serves solely as a technical developer account publisher and organizational entity. <strong>SAVERA CONTINENTAL LIMITED IS NOT LIABLE FOR ANY CONTENT, APPLICATIONS, DATA, CODE, SERVICE MALFUNCTIONS, OMISSIONS, CLAIMS, LOSSES, OR DAMAGES OF ANY KIND WHATSOEVER</strong> arising out of or connected to the Platform or its use.
        </p>

        <hr />

        <div class="section-title">5. User Conduct & Academic Integrity</div>
        <p>
            All users agree to submit only truthful, accurate check-in details corresponding to their actual identity and scheduled period. Falsifying check-in records, spoofing names, evading class attendance, or attempting to compromise the API server is a direct violation of school district rules and academic integrity standards.
        </p>

        <hr />

        <div class="section-title">6. Modifications & Governing Law</div>
        <p>
            These terms may be revised at any time without prior notice. Continued use constitutes full acceptance of revised terms. Any dispute arising in connection with the Platform shall be resolved under the laws of the State of New Jersey, without regard to conflict of law provisions.
        </p>

        <hr />

        <div class="section-title">7. Contact</div>
        <p>
            For questions or concerns, reach out to Kabir Sekhon directly at <a href="mailto:kabsek30@bergen.org">kabsek30@bergen.org</a>.
        </p>
    </main>

    <hr />

    <footer>
        <div>Built and maintained by Kabir Sekhon (ATCS '30).</div>
        <div>&copy; {yearDisplay} Kabir Sekhon. All rights reserved.</div>

        <nav>
            <a href="/terms">Terms of Service</a>
            <span>&middot;</span>
            <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>
            <span>&middot;</span>
            <a href="https://github.com/bca-upper-cafe/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">GitHub</a>
        </nav>
    </footer>

</body>
</html>
